│ 0       │ 'Handler reports a business error (unknown student)'         │ 'result.isError = true'                                      │
│ 1       │ 'Arguments fail the tool inputSchema'                        │ 'result.isError = true'                                      │
│ 2       │ 'Tool name does not exist'                                   │ 'throws ProtocolError (-32602)'                              │
│ 3       │ 'Prompt arguments fail argsSchema'                           │ 'throws ProtocolError (-32602)'                              │
│ 4       │ 'Resource URI not found'                                     │ 'throws ProtocolError (-32602)'                              │
│ 5       │ 'Method not available in this protocol era (ping on 2026)'   │ 'throws SdkError (METHOD_NOT_SUPPORTED_BY_PROTOCOL_VERSION)' │
│ 6       │ 'Connection already closed'                                  │ 'throws Error'                                               │
│ 7       │ 'Request timeout'                                            │ 'throws SdkError (REQUEST_TIMEOUT)'                          │
│ 8       │ 'Capability the server never advertised (prompts on a tools' │ 'normal result'                                              │
└─────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
   ℹ Rule of thumb: tool-level problems come back as a RESULT (isError) so the LLM can read and recover;
   ℹ protocol problems THROW ProtocolError (JSON-RPC code from the server); local problems THROW SdkError.

